The '''Byss Run''' was a [[hyperspace route]] in [[the Interior]] and [[Deep Core]] regions of [[the galaxy]]. It began at the [[planet]] [[Empress Teta]], a junction onto the [[Koros Trunk Line]], and then connected to the planet [[Prakith]], the astronomical object [[Keeara Major system|Keera Major]], and then finally the planet [[Byss]]. It made up part of the larger [[Nexus Route]].

==Description==
The Byss Run was a [[hyperspace route]]<ref name="BMF 36" /> located within [[the Interior]]<ref name="Interior" /> and [[Deep Core]] regions of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Nexus" /> It began with the [[planet]] [[Empress Teta]]<ref name="BMF 36" /> in the [[Empress Teta system]] of the [[Koros sector]]<ref name="Nexus" /> and then passed through<ref name="BMF 36" /> the [[Volcano|volcanic]] planet<ref name="GlassAbyss">''[[Mace Windu: The Glass Abyss]]''</ref> [[Prakith]] and the astronomical object [[Keeara Major system|Keera Major]] before reaching its endpoint at the world [[Byss]].<ref name="BMF 36" /> Empress Teta also acted as a terminus for the [[Koros Trunk Line]] route that ran to the [[Core Worlds]] planet [[Coruscant]] and was also part of the [[Carbonite Run]].<ref name="Nexus" /> Both the Byss Run and the Koros Trunk Line made up sections of the larger [[Nexus Route]]<ref name="NexusRoute">[[Star Wars Galaxy Map (poster)|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map poster]] shows what {{BuildFalconCite|36|Guide to the Galaxy}} identifies as the [[Koros Trunk Line]] and Byss Run as part of a larger route that "[[The Citadel (episode)|The Citadel]]" identifies as the [[Nexus Route]].</ref> which connected Byss to the [[Abregado system]] in the Core Worlds.<ref name="GM">{{GalaxyMapPoster}}</ref>

==History==
One of the earliest [[species]] to inhabit the Byss Run left behind [[color]]ful frescoes from which the designs of the paintings on the cards of the game [[Bakurat]]were derieved.<ref name="Bakurat">{{StoryCite|story=Bakurat (short story)|book=Dark Legends}}</ref> During the [[Clone Wars]], [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] of the Republic&mdash;the public identity of the [[Sith Lord]] Darth Sidious&mdash;provided the coordinates for the secret Nexus Route to [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] [[General]] [[Grievous]]. The general then led the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|Separatist Fleet]] from the [[Outer Rim Territories]] down the length of the route to reach Coruscant and launch a [[Battle of Coruscant|surprise attack]] on the Republic capital<ref name="CloneWars">{{EncyclopediaCite|The End of the Clone Wars}}</ref> in [[19 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref>

In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Starcruiserdate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]] to [[34 ABY]].</ref> [[Chandrila Star Line]]'s [[MPO-1400 Purgill-class star cruiser|Star Cruiser]] ''[[Halcyon]]'' displayed a partial map of the [[galaxy]] that showed the Byss Run on several [[Viewscreen|screens]] while on a cruise from the Core Worlds' [[Chandrila system]] to the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="GS">[[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the Byss Run was first mentioned in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 36|thirty-sixth]] issue of the ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine,<ref name="BMF 36" /> published around [[September 9]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate">{{BuildFalconDates|36}}</ref> The route's first [[in-universe]] appearance came in the form of being depicted on a map viewable in [[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]], an immersive roleplaying experience at [[W:c:disney:Walt Disney World Resort|Walt Disney World Resort]] in Florida<ref name="GS" /> that opened to the public on [[March 1]], [[2022]].<ref name="31 Things">{{SW|url=news/31-things-we-learned-about-star-wars-galactic-starcruiser|text=31 Things We Learned in an Exclusive Preview of ''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser|nolive=1}}</ref>

The [[Byss Run/Legends|Byss Run]] originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first mentioned in the [[Dark Empire II 1|first issue]] of the [[Star Wars comic books|comic book]] series ''[[Star Wars: Dark Empire II]]'', which was written by [[Tom Veitch]], illustrated by [[Cam Kennedy]], and published by [[Dark Horse Comics]]<ref name="DEII1">[[Dark Empire II 1|''Dark Empire II'' 1]]</ref> on [[December 20]], [[1994]].<ref name="Marvel">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/54063/star_wars_dark_empire_ii_1994_1|text=Star Wars: Dark Empire II (1994) #1}}</ref> The route then appeared in the [[Dark Empire II 3|third issue]] of the series,<ref name="DEII3">[[Dark Empire II 3|''Dark Empire II'' 3]]</ref> which was published on [[February 21]], [[1995]].<ref name="Marvel2">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/54065/star_wars_dark_empire_ii_1994_3|text=Star Wars: Dark Empire II (1994) #3}}</ref>

